@startuml Admin_Reports_Management_SSD

actor "Administrator" as Admin
participant "UI: Reports & Analytics" as UI
participant "Database" as DB

== View Reports Dashboard ==

Admin -> UI: Access reports page
activate UI

UI -> DB: Fetch all users data
activate DB
DB --> UI: Return users list
deactivate DB

UI -> DB: Fetch all reviews data
activate DB
DB --> UI: Return reviews list
deactivate DB

UI -> UI: Calculate statistics\n(country, gender, language,\nratings, sites)

UI --> Admin: Display analytics dashboard\n(summary cards + charts)
deactivate UI

== Toggle View Mode ==

Admin -> UI: Click "View Tables" / "View Charts"
activate UI

UI -> UI: Switch between\ncharts view and tables view

UI --> Admin: Display selected view
deactivate UI

== Print Report ==

Admin -> UI: Click "Print Report"
activate UI

UI -> UI: Format data for printing\n(hide controls, show print styles)

UI -> UI: Trigger window.print()

UI --> Admin: Browser print dialog

deactivate UI

== View Activity Logs ==

Admin -> UI: Access logs page
activate UI

UI -> DB: Fetch activity logs
activate DB
DB --> UI: Return logs list (limit 200)
deactivate DB

UI --> Admin: Display logs table\n(paginated, 10 per page)
deactivate UI

== Search and Filter Logs ==

Admin -> UI: Enter search term or select filter
activate UI

UI -> UI: Filter logs by:\n- Search (admin, action, details)\n- Type (review, itinerary, etc.)\n- Sort (latest/oldest)

UI --> Admin: Display filtered results
deactivate UI

== View Log Details ==

Admin -> UI: Click "View Details" on log entry
activate UI

UI --> Admin: Show detail modal\n(full log information)

Admin -> UI: Click "Close"

UI --> Admin: Close modal
deactivate UI

== Print Logs ==

Admin -> UI: Click "Print Logs"
activate UI

UI -> UI: Format logs for printing\n(include all filtered logs,\nhide pagination)

UI -> UI: Trigger window.print()

UI --> Admin: Browser print dialog

deactivate UI

@enduml
